\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The nine families of \cref  {eq:families}, with the crystallography that fixes each one's geometry. $\lambda _k=\sqrt  {\Omega /\pi (\bm  {b}\!\cdot \!\bm  {n})_k}$ is the length converting $\sqrt  {m}$ into a radius, \cref  {eq:radius}. The lattice constants are $a=\SI {0.323}{\nano \meter }$, $c=\SI {0.515}{\nano \meter }$, hence $c/a=1.5944$ --- the physical ratio and not the ideal $\sqrt  {8/3}=1.6330$ --- and $\Omega =(\sqrt  3/4)a^2c=\SI {2.3266e-29}{\cubic \meter }$.}}{6}{}\protected@file@percent }
